#!/bin/sh
# helena-halogen.service's ExecStartPost: the unit counts as started once Halogen answers
# /health with a responding engine, not when the container process exists. Loading the weights
# takes minutes after a boot; the unit's TimeoutStartSec bounds the wait.
#   wait-healthy <port>
port=${1:-8731}
i=0
while :; do
  body=$(curl -fsS --max-time 5 "http://127.0.0.1:$port/health" 2>/dev/null || true)
  case "$body" in
    *'"status":"ok"'*'"responds":true'*|*'"status": "ok"'*'"responds": true'*) exit 0 ;;
  esac
  i=$((i + 1))
  # A note every minute, so the journal shows the wait.
  [ $((i % 30)) -eq 0 ] && echo "halogen: waiting for /health on 127.0.0.1:$port ($((i * 2)) s)"
  sleep 2
done
